From 89965ea7d0aaac0d894f3a6326af9744f7a86f4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Tsao <yang@fydeos.io>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 19:00:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 52/75] wm: don't draw Android's freeform decor for ARC windows
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Chrome draws the caption for every ARC window and owns resizing it, so
Shell's freeform decor is not a second opinion — it is interference, and
invisible interference, because the caption window is NOT_VISIBLE while
still owning input.

It bites in tablet mode, where the window fills the work area and the
decor's strips land on furniture the user needs. Measured on device with a
2560x1520 window, in physical panel coords on the ROT_90 display:

  Embedded{Caption of Task=82}     frame=[1524,0][1600,2560]
      -> logical y 0..76, exactly where ash starts the multitask menu drag
  Embedded{DragResizeInputListener of ...}  one rect [26,40][80,2522]
      -> logical y 1520..1574, over the shelf

Both windows exist only for WINDOWING_MODE_FREEFORM tasks, so they
appeared in tablet mode when the tablet steady state moved to FREEFORM
(device/fydeos 08c179f, which is there to stop Android animating a
layout-mode change). In clamshell the window is inset, so the same
strips sat harmlessly in open screen and nobody noticed them.

shouldShowWindowDecor() gates only decoration lifecycle — onTaskOpening
and onTaskChanging — so returning false creates nothing and tears down
anything that predates the flag. Nothing in device/fydeos references the
decor. persist.fydroid.window_decor=1 restores stock behaviour.

Verified on device by A/B: with the property set, Caption container of
Task=N and DragResizeInputListener appear in the layer tree and claim 4
input windows; with it clear, zero. Flips live, no SystemUI restart.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Id3cfda1cec2d60e50f4076c83bf0845cb7d38bda
---
 .../CaptionWindowDecorViewModel.java          | 23 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libs/WindowManager/Shell/src/com/android/wm/shell/windowdecor/CaptionWindowDecorViewModel.java b/libs/WindowManager/Shell/src/com/android/wm/shell/windowdecor/CaptionWindowDecorViewModel.java
index 6b7ca421f5ed..fd128dcfe493 100644
--- a/libs/WindowManager/Shell/src/com/android/wm/shell/windowdecor/CaptionWindowDecorViewModel.java
+++ b/libs/WindowManager/Shell/src/com/android/wm/shell/windowdecor/CaptionWindowDecorViewModel.java
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@ import static android.app.WindowConfiguration.WINDOWING_MODE_FULLSCREEN;
 import android.app.ActivityManager.RunningTaskInfo;
 import android.content.Context;
 import android.os.Handler;
+import android.os.SystemProperties;
 import android.util.SparseArray;
 import android.view.Choreographer;
 import android.view.MotionEvent;
@@ -145,6 +146,28 @@ public class CaptionWindowDecorViewModel implements WindowDecorViewModel {
     }
 
     private boolean shouldShowWindowDecor(RunningTaskInfo taskInfo) {
+        // fydroid-rt: never. Chrome draws the caption for every ARC window and
+        // owns resizing it, so Android's freeform decor is not a second opinion
+        // — it is interference, and it is invisible interference because the
+        // caption window is NOT_VISIBLE while still owning input.
+        //
+        // It bites hardest in tablet mode, where the window fills the work
+        // area, so the decor's edge strips land on furniture the user needs:
+        // measured on device with a 2560x1520 window, the DragResizeInputListener
+        // claimed UI y 1519-1573 (the shelf) and the caption window claimed UI
+        // y 0-75 — exactly where ash starts the multitask menu drag. In
+        // clamshell the window is inset, so the same strips sit harmlessly in
+        // open screen and nobody noticed them.
+        //
+        // Both windows exist only for WINDOWING_MODE_FREEFORM tasks, so they
+        // appeared in tablet mode when the tablet steady state moved to
+        // FREEFORM (device/fydeos 08c179f, which is there to stop Android
+        // animating a layout-mode change).
+        //
+        // persist.fydroid.window_decor=1 restores the stock behaviour.
+        if (!SystemProperties.getBoolean("persist.fydroid.window_decor", false)) {
+            return false;
+        }
         return taskInfo.getWindowingMode() == WINDOWING_MODE_FREEFORM
                 || (taskInfo.getActivityType() == ACTIVITY_TYPE_STANDARD
                 && taskInfo.configuration.windowConfiguration.getDisplayWindowingMode()
